msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/teleology|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment"
msgid "Goals, desires, intentions, and commitments — the UFO-C intentional-moment trichotomy surfaced as GMEOW core (Principle 16: an agent recording its OWN goals across sessions is a question every AI system will face about itself, alongside identity and deception epistemics).\n\nDOCTRINE.\n  * The trichotomy is commitment-graded: a Desire is wanted but not committed; an Intention is internally committed; a Commitment is socially committed toward another agent. Desire and Intention are intrinsic modes inhering in one agent; a Commitment is a relator mediating at least two.\n  * A Goal is the propositional content — a described state of affairs (gmeow:SocialObject), satisfied by situations via gmeow:satisfiedBy. DOLCE DnS arrives at the same shape independently (goal as a Description satisfied by Situations); the convergence is documented in docs.md.\n  * gmeow:counterGoal is CONSTITUTIVE opposition — the named shadow that partly defines the goal. Strictly stronger than an antonym edge: the counter-goal is part of what the goal means, not merely its lexical opposite.\n  * Whether a situation satisfies a goal is a vantage-indexed claim through the statement layer, never a global verdict (Principle 9). Whose goal it is, is indexed the same way: goals attributed to an agent by an observer and goals avowed by the agent are coexisting claims.\n  * Flat-first, reify on demand (Principle 4): gmeow:hasGoal covers the 80% case; promote to Desire / Intention / Commitment when commitment grade, tenure, or standpoint matters; promote to gmeow:IntentionTenure (the StandpointTenure idiom) when adoption / revision of the intention is itself the fact of interest. Goals are revised by suppression, never deleted (Principle 10).\n  * Goals and authored dependency relations are ontology data. Choosing a decomposition, plan search, and means-end reasoning are solver-layer computations (Principle 12); the ontology retains the goals, dependencies, counter-goals, and attributed holders that those computations consume.\n  * Deontic force lives elsewhere: a Goal prescribes nothing. Norms that make conduct obligatory arrive with the core norms slice, which ranges gmeow:prescribedConduct over Goal — the dependency points norms → teleology, never back."
msgstr "目标、愿望、意向与承诺：UFO-C 意向性依存体的三分法以 GMEOW 核心词汇呈现（原则 16：代理跨会话记录自身目标，是每个 AI 系统都会面对的自我问题，与身份和欺骗认识论并列）。\n\n基本准则。\n  * 三分法按承诺程度区分：Desire 表示有所期望但尚未承诺；Intention 表示内部承诺；Commitment 表示对另一代理的社会承诺。Desire 与 Intention 是依存于单个代理的内在模态；Commitment 是至少联结两个参与者的关系实体。\n  * Goal 是命题内容，即所描述的事态（gmeow:SocialObject），由情境通过 gmeow:satisfiedBy 满足。DOLCE DnS 独立采用相同结构：目标是由 Situations 满足的 Description。docs.md 说明这一趋同。\n  * gmeow:counterGoal 表示构成性的对立，即部分定义目标的具名对立面。它比反义关系更强：反目标是目标含义的一部分，而非仅仅是词汇上的相反表达。\n  * 情境是否满足目标，是通过陈述层表达的视角索引断言，绝非全局裁决（原则 9）。目标归属也按相同方式索引：观察者归于代理的目标与代理自行声明的目标可以并存。\n  * 先用简单关系，按需实体化（原则 4）：gmeow:hasGoal 覆盖常见情况；当承诺程度、持有期间或立场重要时，采用 Desire / Intention / Commitment；当意向的采纳或修订本身就是所关注的事实时，采用 StandpointTenure 模式中的 gmeow:IntentionTenure。目标通过抑制显示来修订，绝不删除（原则 10）。\n  * 目标及所编写的依赖关系都是本体数据。选择分解方案、规划搜索和手段目的推理属于求解器层计算（原则 12）；本体保留这些计算所使用的目标、依赖关系、反目标和所归属的持有者。\n  * 义务效力属于其他领域：Goal 本身不作规定。使行为具有义务性的规范由核心 norms 切片提供，该切片将 gmeow:prescribedConduct 的值域设为 Goal；依赖方向是 norms 到 teleology，绝不反向。"
